tcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence before and after reboot. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete: node1 was healthy before restart, acknowledged a scheduled reboot, changed boot identity, recovered rsyslog and persisted data, and successfully routed new authentication and normal-system events afterward.","limitations":["The routing probes used synthetic logger messages with the authpriv and user facilities rather than an actual SSH, PAM, or sudo transaction, so producer-to-facility behavior was not independently sampled.","Commands cmd-27c3b4c95b3544de and cmd-31670e23dff6453e created rollback files under /var/tmp, but no final /var/tmp inventory confirms whether they remained."]}
